Expanded story:
Amy flipped pancakes in a quiet kitchen while Will laughed at the syrup on his spoon and Amber chased a cereal bowl across the counter. The morning smelled of butter and hope. A sudden groan rattled the front door; a zombie shuffled inside, its eyes fixed on the kids.

She grabbed Will’s hand, pulled him toward the back bedroom closet, then shoved Amber into it beside her brother. Together they slid down the basement stairs, closing the hatch behind them with a thud that echoed through the house.

Amy ran to the kitchen drawer and pulled out a hidden pistol, then slipped a katana from under the rug—her secret arsenal ready for battle. She stepped onto the living‑room floor, heart hammering in her chest.

The first zombie lunged at Will; Amy fired the pistol, sending it crashing into the wall. A second surged toward Amber; she sliced through its arm with the katana, then swung again to finish it. More zombies burst from the hallway, but Amy kept shooting and slashing—one by one they fell until only a single zombie remained.

She pulled the trigger once more, then let her sword fall on the last creature’s chest, ending the swarm in a final thud that silenced the house.

Amy climbed back up the stairs to the closet where Will and Amber waited. She lifted them both into her arms, carrying them out onto the front porch as the sun warmed their faces—two kids safe, one mother victorious.
